{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#2839","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#2839","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#2839\",\"parent_revision\":\"6112474fe4253b6dc64d48dd2845f9321c7bc5f4a0dce436f90bf86b3cea82b4\",\"root_revision\":\"6112474fe4253b6dc64d48dd2845f9321c7bc5f4a0dce436f90bf86b3cea82b4\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: \\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## Root Cause Genuinely Unknown No Confirmed Hypothesis\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAn initial version of this issue speculated that `test_l2` fails due to GitHub GraphQL search-index eventual-consistency lag between `test_l1` creating an issue and `test_l2` listing it. **That speculation has been checked against the actual code and does not hold up**: `backlog_list` \u2192 `sync_issues_graphql` \u2192 `_fetch_issues_graphql` (`plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/gh_client.py:564-629`) queries the GraphQL `repository.issues` connection, not GitHub's Search API (`search(query: ...)`). The documented indexing-lag behavior applies to Search specifically; `repository.issues` reads the same primary store that `backlog_add`'s REST write goes through. There is no verified evidence this connection has read-after-write lag, so this explanation is retracted, not confirmed.\\n\\nRoot cause for both `test_l2` and `test_l8` is **unknown**. Do not act on any hypothesis here without a captured traceback first.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Root Cause: Genuinely Unknown \u2014 No Confirmed Hypothesis\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAn initial version of this issue speculated that `test_l2` fails due to GitHub GraphQL search-index eventual-consistency lag between `test_l1` creating an issue and `test_l2` listing it. **That speculation has been checked against the actual code and does not hold up**: `backlog_list` \u2192 `sync_issues_graphql` \u2192 `_fetch_issues_graphql` (`plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/gh_client.py:564-629`) queries the GraphQL `repository.issues` connection, not GitHub's Search API (`search(query: ...)`). The documented indexing-lag behavior applies to Search specifically; `repository.issues` reads the same primary store that `backlog_add`'s REST write goes through. There is no verified evidence this connection has read-after-write lag, so this explanation is retracted, not confirmed.\\n\\nRoot cause for both `test_l2` and `test_l8` is **unknown**. Do not act on any hypothesis here without a captured traceback first.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Root Diagnostic Gap\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n`pytest-timeout` is not a dependency and no per-test timeout is configured anywhere (`pyproject.toml`, `conftest.py`, or the test file). When one test hangs, the outer GitHub Actions `timeout-minutes: 10` on the whole step is the only thing that eventually kills it \u2014 and it kills the whole process tree before pytest reaches its end-of-session `FAILURES` summary, so **no traceback is ever captured** for any failure in the same run. This is why the current failure has no assertion detail: only the xdist live `FAILED` line survived.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Suggested First Step\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAdd `pytest-timeout` and a per-test timeout (e.g. 60\u201390s) scoped to `test_live_validation.py` so a hung test fails with its own traceback instead of consuming the whole step budget and erasing diagnostics for every other test in the run. Only after that captures a real traceback should a root-cause investigation for `test_l2`/`test_l8` begin \u2014 per this repo's `fix-delegation-discipline.md`, no fix should be attempted without a reproduction and evidence in hand.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Problem\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nDiscovered while verifying the `DH_ALLOW_TEST_NETWORK` fix in #2837 (manual `workflow_dispatch` run: https://github.com/Jamie-BitFlight/claude_skills/actions/runs/31371440005/job/93401106053). With the network guard correctly lifted, the E2E suite ran against the live GitHub sandbox and:\\n\\n- `test_l2_list_includes_created_item` \u2014 **FAILED** (no traceback captured, see below)\\n- `test_l1`, `test_l3`\u2013`test_l7` \u2014 passed\\n- `test_l8_sync_push_groomed` \u2014 started at 08:52:49, never completed; the whole `Run e2e tests` step hit its 10-minute `timeout-minutes` limit at 08:55:17 and was killed\\n\\n`Emergency cleanup (always runs)` executed correctly afterward and swept 1 orphaned `[MCP-TEST-` issue \u2014 cleanup itself is not in question.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Success Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n`test_l2_list_includes_created_item` and `test_l8_sync_push_groomed` pass in a `workflow_dispatch` run of `Code quality`, or (if a genuine, evidenced consistency/timing constraint is found) an appropriate retry/wait is added with a documented, evidence-backed reason.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Reproduce\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n```bash\\nDH_ALLOW_TEST_NETWORK=1 GITHUB_TOKEN=<token> GITHUB_REPO=Jamie-BitFlight/claude_skills \\\\\\n  uv run -q pytest -m e2e -v plugins/development-harness/tests/test_live_validation.py\\n```\\n\\nOr via `workflow_dispatch` on `Code quality` (now enabled \u2014 see #2837).\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"f375ad2520125e94384ca8663ef82e727440e9a3fbe3a50ddffd46223b70fa96\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABSdqNPg\"}"}